/**
 * Machine-prerequisite sync backing `sandbox setup`.
 *
 * The prerequisites of the sandbox system live outside this repo and outside
 * any workspace, on the developer's machine:
 *
 *   * the **registry configs** in `~/.sandbox` (services.yaml, ports.yaml,
 *     model-pricing.yaml, secrets.env) — seeded from lib/scaffold on a fresh
 *     machine, migrated up from a legacy `infra/config/` checkout when one is
 *     found, and never overwritten once they exist;
 *   * the **ingress certificate** covering every hostname the registry routes,
 *     generated by `bin/generate-certs.sh`;
 *   * the **sandbox-tools plugin** (user scope, from the `sandbox` marketplace
 *     this repo serves at `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`) — carries the
 *     sandbox-* ops skills;
 *   * the **ponytail plugin** (user scope) — the sb-* entry skills reference
 *     it, with graceful fallback, so absence degrades rather than breaks;
 *   * the **superpowers plugin** (user scope, OPTIONAL) — installed only when
 *     the wizard asks and the answer is yes. Nothing references it, so a
 *     decline is reported ok rather than as drift;
 *   * the **companion sandbox-workspace checkout** under the repos root —
 *     `sandbox workspace` creates each workspace root as a worktree of it
 *     (plain-directory fallback with a warning when it is missing). Which repo
 *     that is comes from `overrides.workspace_repo`, defaulting to the
 *     authenticated GitHub user's own `<user>/sandbox-workspace`;
 *   * the **Jira API token** in the `jira:` section of ~/.sandbox/config.yaml
 *     (OPTIONAL) — the sandbox-dashboard server's fast path for Jira reads;
 *     absent means it falls back to the claude CLI, so a missing/unfilled token
 *     is reported ok with guidance, and only a filled-but-rejected token fails
 *     the step;
 *   * the **Telepresence OSS client** (OPTIONAL) — installed via Homebrew on
 *     request, since only `sandbox intercept` needs it.
 *
 * This module inspects each and (unless check-only) shells out to
 * `claude plugin …` / `git …` / `brew …` to converge. Philosophy matches
 * plugin_check.ts: report loudly, fail soft — a failed step becomes a not-ok
 * line in the report, never an exception. Check-only mode never writes and
 * runs only read-only probes.
 *
 * NOTHING HERE PROMPTS. The wizard in commands/setup.ts collects answers and
 * passes them in as options, which keeps every step callable — and testable —
 * without a TTY.
 *
 * Unlike plugin_check (which stays silent when Claude's plugin state is
 * unreadable, because a false alarm on every init trains people to ignore
 * it), this module treats absent state as a fresh machine and converges it —
 * `sandbox setup` only runs when explicitly invoked.
 */

